course: dictionary
lesson: 16053
title: Words for people and their jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you who a person is by what they do. A violinist is a person who plays the violin. The ending -ist often means someone who does or plays a certain thing.
explain: «Mia is learning the violin, and she wants to be a violinist one day.» The words one day tell you Mia is not a violinist yet. She is still learning. Context clues like this help you work out who the word is about.
explain: «The famous violinist played to a packed concert hall.» Famous and played tell you a violinist can perform for many people. Some violinists are learners in school orchestras, and some are professionals who play on stage.
fact: A violin is a stringed instrument. You hold it under your chin and play it with a bow.
fact: «Violinist» means a person who plays the violin.
fact: Violinists play in school orchestras and in famous orchestras and bands.
fact: The leading violinist of an orchestra is called the leader in the UK, or the concertmaster in the US.
fact: The plural of violinist is violinists: one violinist, many violinists.
exercise: «Mia is learning the violin, and she wants to be a violinist one day.» What is a violinist? | A case that holds a violin | A person who sells instruments | A tune played on the piano | *A person who plays the violin
exercise: What is the leading violinist of an orchestra called in the US? | *concertmaster | leader | soloist | conductor
exercise: Find and copy the word that names a person who plays the violin. | *violinist | bow | orchestra | violin
test: «The first violinist tuned her instrument before the concert began.» What does first violinist mean here? | A person who sings in the choir | The person who made the violin | A violinist who has just started learning | *The leading violinist of the orchestra
test: Which word is the plural of violinist? | *violinists | violinster | violins | violinest
exam: A violinist holds the violin under her chin and plays it with what? | a piano key | *a bow | a microphone | a drumstick
